schedule: Float as float, Int as long, work-group 256, products and transposes untiled
buffers:
  b_v: long 5 items, %v i64 [5]; input v, uploaded by the host
  b_m: long 9 items, %m i64 [3 3]; input m, uploaded by the host
  b_addr: long 3 items, %addr i64 [3]; written on the device
  b_mul: long 5 items, %mul i64 [5]; written on the device
  b_addr_2: long 1 item, %addr_2 i64 []; written on the device
  b_t: long 9 items, %t i64 [3 3]; written on the device
  b_mm: long 9 items, %mm i64 [3 3]; written on the device
kernels:
  reduce_axis_add_long: along one axis, one work-item per result item folding its line from the right; computes %addr
  k0: 5 elements, one work-item each; computes %mul; writes %mul
  reduce_add_long: a tree reduction in local memory, one partial per work-group; computes %addr_2
  transpose3: 9 elements, one work-item each; computes %t; writes %t
  matmul_long: sums of products, one work-item per result item, folded from the right; computes %mm
  k2: 5 elements, one work-item each; computes %f %div; writes nothing
launches:
  1: reduce_axis_add_long(b_m, b_addr, 3, 3, 1) global 4 local 4: %addr: add along axis 2: 3 lines of 3, one work-item each
  2: k0(b_v, b_mul) global 8 local 8: 5 elements (1 group of 8)
  3: reduce_add_long(b_mul, b_addr_2, 5, local 2048 bytes) global 256 local 256: %addr_2: add 5 items to 1 partial (pass 1)
  4: transpose3(b_m, b_t) global 16 local 16: %t: o_\, the axes reversed, [3 3] to [3 3], 9 items gathered
  5: matmul_long(b_m, b_t, b_mm, 3, 3, 3) global 16 local 16: %mm: 3 by 3 times 3 by 3, 9 sums of 3 products, one work-item each
  6: k2(b_v) global 8 local 8: 5 elements (1 group of 8)
outputs:
  %addr from b_addr, read back by the host
  %addr_2 from b_addr_2, read back by the host
  %mm from b_mm, read back by the host
